# reproducibility; uncomment if your project prefers floating gem versions.
# Gemfile.user.lock

# Workspace session notes (per-session, not versioned)
**/.session-notes
# .session-notes.migrated is produced by the SessionStart hook when a legacy
# monolithic .session-notes is split per-operator
# (.claude/hooks/lib/session-notes-layout.js::MIGRATED_MONOLITH_NAME). The
# loom-managed coc:gitignore_additions block below covers .session-notes,
# .session-notes.d/ and .session-notes.shared.md but NOT this variant, so a
# hook-produced session-notes monolith sits unignored in a PUBLIC template
# repo. Kept HERE (repo-owned region, above the managed markers) so it is
# durable across /sync-to-use; the tier-wide fix is proposed to loom in
# .claude/.proposals/latest.yaml. Remove once the managed block covers it.
.session-notes.migrated
**/.session-notes.migrated
# .wave-tracker.d/ holds the per-operator wave DETAIL that `commands/wrapup.md`
# § Wave tracker and `rules/burn-down-reporting.md` MUST-3 both describe as
# living in "the gitignored `.wave-tracker.d/<display_id>.md`" — but the
# loom-managed coc:gitignore_additions block below covers .session-notes,
# .session-notes.d/ and .session-notes.shared.md and NOT this sibling, so the
# asserted gitignore did not exist and a wave tracker sat unignored in a PUBLIC
# template repo. It carries operator session detail (agent IDs, launch ledger,
# in-flight state) exactly as .session-notes.d/ does. Same class as the
# .session-notes.migrated gap above: a fact asserted at the rule surface and
# never enforced at the authority. Kept HERE (repo-owned region, above the
# managed markers) so it is durable across /sync-to-use; the tier-wide fix is
# proposed to loom in .claude/.proposals/latest.yaml. Remove once the managed
# block covers it.
.wave-tracker.d/
**/.wave-tracker.d/

# .claude/cross-repo-authz/ holds /cross-repo-authorize receipts, which carry
# the authorizing operator's display_id (`requester:`) by design. The ceremony
# (repo-scope-discipline.md § Affordance step 5) says to COMMIT them for
# durable team audit — correct in a normal repo, WRONG here: this is a PUBLIC
# GitHub template (isTemplate:true) that clients clone, so committing a receipt
# ships operator identity into every client fork. Same class as the roster
# contamination vector. Kept HERE (repo-owned region, above the loom-managed
# markers) so it is durable across /sync-to-use. Tier-wide fix proposed to loom
# in .claude/.proposals/latest.yaml; remove this once that lands.
.claude/cross-repo-authz/

# Per-project learning data (generated at runtime)
.claude/learning/
.claude/rules/learned-instincts.md

# Per-operator local identity + runtime telemetry (operator-local; NEVER committed/synced)
# .claude/operator-id contains GPG verified_id fingerprint per multi-operator-coordination.md;
# .claude/logs/ carries telemetry (coc-telemetry-autocommit.log etc.) per knowledge-convergence.md
.claude/operator-id
.claude/logs/

# Operator-local deployment-value siblings (same disclosure class as .claude/operator-id).
# Convention: <file>.operator.local.<ext> + <file>.local.<ext> hold deployment-specific
# values (org slugs, runner hostnames, resolver path overrides). The paired
# <file>.local.example.<ext> / <file>.operator.local.example.<ext> SCHEMAS stay tracked
# — they are the operator-facing templates. Narrow per-dir patterns chosen so audit
# fixtures under .claude/audit-fixtures/**/*.operator.local.* (intended-tracked) are
# NOT over-ignored.
.claude/rules/*.operator.local.md
.claude/bin/*.local.json

# CC worktree-isolation per-operator session state (one subdir per agent)
.claude/worktrees/

# Internal docs (not for distribution)
/docs/01-kailash-vibe-cc-internals/

# Generated script outputs (sdk-users examples)
**/scripts/data/
**/scripts/outputs/
**/scripts/*.log

